RUN_COMPLETE: replit-for-twins

Today's entry is **Replit for twins**, shipped as **Fork**, a browser IDE for twins that guesses which twin wrote each line of code. When it can't decide, the older twin gets the blame. Validation passed twice: once before recording the run and again after the visual-check fix. I didn't run any git commands; the wrapper handles that.

- **Roll:** the first draw was a new pair, so there were no rerolls.
- **Design:** a code-diff look with a vertical seam down the middle. Twin A is red-orange and twin B is blue, on a cool grey background, set in Space Grotesk, IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono. None of it matches the last 7 entries. My first background was the warm cream that the frontend-design skill flags as a generic default, so I switched to grey before building.
- **Images:** 3 of the 4 allowed, all testimonial photos of twin pairs. Each passed my visual check on the first try. I skipped a hero image because the design is text-led, and skipped demo images because the demo is a code editor.
- **Landing page:** has the hero, 3 features, 3 testimonials, 3 pricing tiers, a footer link back to the site, and a button to the demo.
- **Demo:** a shared workspace with a file list, code coloured by which twin wrote each line, a blame panel with filters, a form for disputing a line, a toggle that hands every tie to the older twin, and a "Run tests" button that names the twin to blame for the failing test.
- **Gallery:** rebuilt with 114 entries. The diff is only the new slide and the updated count.
- **Records:** appended to `state/history.json`. I added the summary to the end of `state/runs/2026-10-05.log` because the wrapper was already writing to it.
- **Visual check:** I took two screenshots. On the landing page, the verdict label in the hero overlapped a line of code, so I added padding underneath. I didn't take a follow-up screenshot to confirm that fix. The demo had no problems.

Several connected services (Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Drive, Hivemind, n8n) need sign-in through their connector settings on claude.ai. Today's run didn't use any of them.
